        (id: 302, board: "03", subject: "payphone on 9th calls back", date: "04/11/1998", author: "crankshaft", body: r#"
crankshaft:
the payphone at the gas station on 9th. if you hang up on it,
it calls you back. not the number you called. the payphone.

kestrel:
i tried it. it rang. i picked up. dial tone.

crankshaft:
that's the fun part. it's the dial tone of a different payphone.

mara:
please stop prank calling the infrastructure.
"#),
        (id: 303, board: "03", subject: "numbers that shouldn't ring", date: "05/30/1998", author: "kestrel", body: r#"
kestrel:
collecting weird numbers. add yours.

  555-0199   dial tone, but slightly flat
  555-0123   a man reading weather for a city that doesn't exist
  555-0188   modem carrier, never negotiates
  555-0142   DEADLINE. after 3:17am: two rings, then breathing.

byte_witch:
the deadline one is just line noise

kestrel:
probably.

byte_witch:
...probably.
"#),
        (
            id: 304,
            board: "03",
            subject: "the old commands",
            date: "06/09/1998",
            author: "ghost_17",
            body: r#"
ghost_17:
for the new people: this board still answers {cyan}trace <user>{/}
and {cyan}scan{/}. mara never ripped them out.

use them. don't abuse them. and don't trace ROOT, it hates that.

mara:
i don't hate anything. ROOT doesn't exist yet.

ghost_17:
yet.
"#,
            on_read: [If(NoFlag("knows_trace"), [Set("knows_trace"), Log("shell: trace, scan available")], [])],
        ),
        (id: 305, board: "03", subject: "2600hz and you: a love story", date: "06/20/1998", author: "byte_witch", body: r#"
byte_witch:
my little brother got a toy whistle out of a cereal box and
blew it into the phone. nothing happened. he was very upset.
i told him it was 1971 for exactly one person and it wasn't him.

dialtone:
i would like to subscribe to more cereal facts
"#),
